From ce7d43383ffa19be2c070b2e21a754ee854c666e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move thumbnail sizing out of JS and into globals.css
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The control now sets one class on the grid container and nothing else:
size-1 … size-5. No inline grid-template-columns, no pixel values in the
component, no computed style attribute. Everything about how big a
thumbnail is lives in one commented block in globals.css.

Two modifiers, because the two grids have nothing in common but the
control. .photo-grid--page is the gallery, sized by target tile width so
the column count falls out of the space available between a phone and
max-w-5xl. .photo-grid--panel is the map panel, sized by explicit column
count — its width ranges from a phone-width sheet to an 880px side panel,
and counting columns is the only way every press of + changes something
at the narrow end. Tile aspect ratio moves there too, as .photo-tile.

The align-content: start that stops the panel flattening its rows is now
a documented line in that block rather than a utility class buried in a
component.

STEP_COUNT in tile-size.ts is the only thing that still has to agree with
the stylesheet, and it's commented as such.
